    "_comment_new_types": "T3-CREATURES. Ten moves for the five types the owner's creature-expansion brief brings into the Meadows. Two per type -- one quick, one charged -- because a dual-typed creature whose moves are both its PRIMARY type wears its second type as pure defence and the player never sees it; Nightburrow throwing a Dark move is the only way Ground/Dark reads as anything at all. Powers sit in the SPECIES band (0.95-1.10), not the TM ladder (1.15-2.0): these are birth moves, and a creature the player catches should not arrive holding a reward-economy multiplier. Balance note worth keeping: data/config/type_chart.json authors NO matchup rows for these five types, so every one of these moves resolves at exactly 1.0 against every defender. They are strictly LESS swingy than a ground/water/air move, never more -- a wild Stormtrail's Electric attack cannot roll 1.25 into anything, and neither can the player's once it is caught. Identity therefore lives in the timing and reach numbers rather than in effectiveness: electric has the lowest windup of any quick in this file (0.11), psychic the highest and the longest quick reach, ice the longest charged lunge, fire the only `area` quick. `vfx.colour` follows the move's type as this file's header rule requires, each taken from that creature's own palette swatch on the owner's sheets in docs/art/reference/creature-expansion-2026-08-30/.",

