  "_comment_vfx": "`vfx.kind` is how the move reads on screen: `melee` (impact only, at the target), `projectile` (a travelling bolt drawn from the attacker to the target, arriving as the impact plays), `cone` (a spreading wash) and `area` (a ring centred on the attacker). `colour` is the elemental tint and follows the move's type, so ground/water/air stay tellable apart at a glance. The hit itself is still resolved instantly by the same cone arithmetic (owner's call: a visible projectile, not a dodgeable object) -- the travel time only delays the IMPACT, never the damage."
